<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>candidate-brief.md</title><style>body{font:18px system-ui;line-height:1.6;max-width:1000px;margin:2rem auto;padding:1rem;color:#17252d;background:white}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}table{border-collapse:collapse}td,th{border:1px solid #777;padding:.5rem}a{color:#064b8c}</style><main><h1>Specify a monthly close-file preparation routine — learner brief</h1>
<p>Fictional Northstar Services training material.</p>
<h2>Current and future process</h2>
<p>Receive 10 min, inspect names/periods 10, create index 10, review completeness 15.
Proposed run 3, review 15, recovery 5 min. Fictional estimates.
Files: EAST-2026-09-AP.pdf; WEST-2026-09-AR.pdf; EAST-2026-08-AP.pdf; unlabelled.pdf.
Run September. Read filenames, write new draft index only. No deletion, approval, sending.</p>
<h2>Task</h2>
<p>Northstar repeatedly renames and indexes close support files. Scope a routine that creates a draft index without approving the support.</p>
<h2>Actions</h2>
<ol>
<li>Map the four current steps and mark review completeness as retained human work.</li>
<li>Ask AI for an input contract and an output-only routine specification.</li>
<li>Define accepted filename parts (unit, period, support type) and reject ambiguous names.</li>
<li>Trace all four filenames for a September run, recording two current-period candidates and two exceptions.</li>
<li>Compare 45 minutes baseline with 23 minutes proposed total and label the 22-minute difference an untested scenario estimate.</li>
<li>Write a stop condition for missing or ambiguous inputs.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Output</h2>
<p>Current/future steps; trigger; filename contract; allowed/blocked actions; owner; tabletop disposition; time comparison.</p>
</main></html>